<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Drafts is where text starts for me, and has been for years. Get the words down, then decide where they belong. Version 54 adds a Chat Console for working with that text and more control over dictation.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <a href="https://docs.getdrafts.com/docs/actions/console">new Chat Console</a> handles one-off jobs inside the app. Ask it to sort a grocery list by sections of the store, or make a summary of your flagged drafts. Drafts gives the model tools to find and work with the text in your library and editor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A small job doesn&#8217;t have to become a scripting project, and your existing actions are still there for routines you want to repeat. Start with a simple request and check the result before keeping the changes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The console requires Drafts 54 or later, Drafts Pro, and iOS or macOS 27 or later on a device with Apple Intelligence supported and enabled. Each chat is temporary; Drafts doesn&#8217;t keep a chat history.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Pay attention to the model you choose. Apple&#8217;s on-device model keeps data local but has limited capabilities. Apple&#8217;s Private Cloud Compute runs remotely, and third-party models need a separately billed API key.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <a href="https://docs.getdrafts.com/docs/editor/dictation">updated dictation interface</a> on OS 27 adds custom dictionaries for the names and terms you say often. A word like MacSparky is a good example. Add it to a dictionary to give speech recognition a hint about what you mean.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can pause, make a correction in the preview, and resume before saving the text. Dictation can also continue in the background, with an iOS Live Activity showing that it&#8217;s still listening.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Drafts uses Apple&#8217;s speech APIs. Local, offline dictation is supported in many cases, but availability depends on your device and language. Some setups still need a network connection.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The current 54.1 update adds compatibility fixes and improves the dictation Live Activity&#8217;s appearance. Chat Console and the new dictation interface arrived with 54.0.</p>



